  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A real dog paradise on the French Riviera: on the two Lérins islands, every beach and cove is accessible to dogs kept on a leash. More than 28 spots have been recorded across Sainte-Marguerite and Saint-Honorat, plenty to vary your walks on each visit.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access is only by ferry from the port of Cannes — remember to check that your chosen ferry company accepts dogs on board, and plan to arrive early in summer to avoid the crowds on the first crossings.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Sainte-Marguerite is larger and wilder, ideal for a proper forest walk before the swim — Saint-Honorat, with its abbey, is quieter but smaller.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The port of Cannes, the departure point for the ferries, is full of terraces for a break before or after the crossing.</p>
